<%#
  §17 — the auth frame, opened.

  "Scaffolding tools generate ugly forms. These screens must match the rest
  of the product." So this is not a card floating on a page: it is a sheet
  with crop marks, the same object every other screen in the product is.

  No social login buttons. §17 — passkeys are the modern path, and a wall of
  coloured OAuth buttons would wreck the page.

  Every value below is printed through EJS's escaping output tag rather
  than concatenated into a string, so output escaping is the default and
  not a thing anyone has to remember (§13.3).
%>
<%- include('../partials/head', { title: title }) %>
<main class="sheet auth-sheet">
  <span class="crop tl" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  <span class="crop tr" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  <span class="crop bl" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  <span class="crop br" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  <div class="auth-block" id="block">
    <a class="auth-mark mono-s" href="/">MARGIN</a>
